## Original Content
The support will benefit children in three Sudanese states; West Darfur, South Kordofan and Gedaref with the aim of restoring “safe, quality and inclusive education” amid the world's largest humanitarian and displacement crisis.

## Summary
The UN has launched a $22 million education initiative to support children in West Darfur, South Kordofan, and Gedaref states in Sudan. The program aims to restore safe, quality, and inclusive education amid the world's largest humanitarian and displacement crisis.

## Key Points
- UN launched a $22m education initiative for Sudan's children.
- Initiative benefits children in three states: West Darfur, South Kordofan, and Gedaref.
- Goal is to restore safe, quality, and inclusive education.
- Addresses a major humanitarian and displacement crisis.


